---
/**
 * 官网服务条款（与当前产品实现对齐；非律师意见书）。
 */
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro'
import '../styles/pages.css'

const effectiveDate = '2026-10-18'
const contactEmail = 'privacy@yiveno.com'
---

<MainLayout
  title="Terms of Service · Yiveno"
  description="Terms of Service for the Yiveno Chromium extension (Microsoft Edge and Google Chrome) and website."
>
  <article class="page">
    <header>
      <h1 class="page__title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="page__meta">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="page__prose" lang="en">
      <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        By using Yiveno (the Chromium browser extension for Microsoft Edge and Google Chrome, the
        website, and related services), you agree to these Terms and our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Yiveno is currently operated by an <strong>individual</strong> based in{' '}
        <strong>Hangzhou, China</strong>. Operations may later move to a company registered in
        Hangzhou; we will update these Terms if that happens.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The service</h2>
      <p>
        Yiveno helps you <strong>capture and recall personal browsing traces</strong> (excerpts,
        notes, and related metadata you choose to save). It is not sold as a bookmark manager, note
        editor, chat bot, or general “AI life assistant.” Features marked unavailable in the product
        are not promised. The browser extension is <strong>not yet publicly listed</strong> on the
        Chrome Web Store or Microsoft Edge Add-ons, and paid plans are{' '}
        <strong>not yet offered to the public</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You may use local-only features without signing in. If you sign in, you must keep your
        credentials secure and provide accurate account information. Signing in does not by itself
        upload memories; cloud sync is opt-in in the extension. You may delete your account from
        Settings → Privacy as described in the product.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You retain rights to content you Capture. You grant us a limited license to host and process
        that content only as needed to provide the features you enable (including optional cloud
        sync and AI assistance routed through our Worker). You must not use Yiveno to store or
        transmit unlawful material.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Do not abuse, disrupt, or reverse-engineer the service beyond permitted interoperability
        </li>
        <li>Do not attempt unauthorized access to others’ accounts or data</li>
        <li>Do not use the service in ways that violate applicable law</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Paid plans</h2>
      <p>
        Paid plans (for example Pro) may be described on the website for future availability. As of
        the effective date above, we are <strong>not yet charging</strong> the public. If and when
        you purchase a subscription, billing is handled by our payment provider. Fees, renewal, and
        cancellation follow the checkout terms shown at purchase. We may retain billing records as
        required by law after account deletion.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        The service is provided “as is.” Recall results and AI-assisted understanding are
        probabilistic aids; they do not guarantee correctness. We do not warrant uninterrupted or
        error-free operation.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, Yiveno and its operators are not liable for
        indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, or for loss of data beyond what the
        product’s local/cloud controls allow you to export or delete. Some jurisdictions do not
        allow certain limitations; those limits apply only to the extent allowed.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms. We will change the effective date on this page. Continued use
        after changes means you accept the updated Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Product support and complaints: <a href="/support">Support</a>(
        <a href="mailto:support@yiveno.com">support@yiveno.com</a>). Privacy:
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="page__note">
        This page is not legal advice. It reflects how Yiveno is offered today.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</MainLayout>
